source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: The delimiter a row closes on leaves no cell behind it: Jira renders `|a||` as the single data cell `a` rather than as `a` and an empty second cell.
-- input.jira --
|a||
-- rendered.html --
<div class='table-wrap'>
<table class='confluenceTable'><tbody>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>a</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>
-- want.md --
:::table
|a||
:::
-- warnings.json --
[]
